using the shared system-browser flow and secure pending-save/confirmation protocol.
It MUST NOT silently replace public sign-in or infer permission from inherited scopes.
The UI MUST explain GitHub's broader repository grant and Pully's current read-only
use, preserve the connected public account on denied/failed consent, and show no
private-access success before server confirmation. Source: Tavi's explicit 22 Oct
private repository request and the reviewed separate repository-consent protocol.
